@startuml
title Circuit state, deadlines and traffic admission
skinparam shadowing false
[*] --> Closed
Closed : Calls admitted subject to capacity
Closed : Healthy completion resets failure count
Closed --> Open : failure threshold reached
Open : Reject calls without provider I/O
Open : Monotonic cooldown clock
Open --> HalfOpen : cooldown elapsed; first eligible call
HalfOpen : Exactly one recovery probe
HalfOpen : Reject other callers
HalfOpen --> Closed : probe healthy and within latency limit
HalfOpen --> Open : failure, slowness, timeout, cancellation or no capacity
note right of Closed
Every call has an asyncio deadline.
Slow completed responses are discarded.
Transport, schema and response failures count.
Policy rejection and busy admission do not count.
end note
note bottom of Open
An epoch prevents a late success from closing
a circuit tripped by a newer failure.
Shared specialist generation circuit; separate judge circuit.
Evaluation auditor has its own circuit and one in-flight slot.
No retries or alternate-provider data transfer.
end note
legend bottom
1. ContextStore: per-owner rate and one turn per session.
2. Chatbot: global in-flight turn cap, no waiting queue.
3. CircuitBreaker: role capacity, deadline, slow threshold, cooldown.
All controls are process-local, not distributed traffic management.
endlegend
footer Agentic Drink Book | Policy 2.1.0 | Model judgments remain fallible
@enduml
